{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1042","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1042","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1042\",\"parent_revision\":\"a29529f1be3b70bd58f24dfb04e8dc9f75475e83\",\"root_revision\":\"fb1fac6a621d2bf0b246ba254718eeb00631ada5c0c6568d0e778ed8794c7c8c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nCodebase analysis artifacts should be incremental and anchored to a git commit SHA so that re-analysis only processes files changed since the prior analysis commit.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **incremental commit-anchored codebase analysis** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User request 2026-03-24\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\nFunctional intent: PRESENT \u2014 make `codebase-analyzer` incremental by anchoring analysis artifacts to a git commit SHA and diffing against HEAD on re-run.\\n\\n**Available**:\\n- Artifact model: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` (contains `ArtifactEntry` schema)\\n- Agent: `plugins/development-harness/agents/codebase-analyzer.md`\\n- `artifact_register`, `artifact_list`, `artifact_read` MCP tools already in use\\n- `git diff {sha}..HEAD --name-only` command well-defined\\n- File exclusion pattern list fully specified in item description\\n\\n**Gap 1 \u2014 Schema location unconfirmed**: Whether `commit_sha` is added to `ArtifactEntry` in `models.py` or to a separate manifest field must be confirmed by reading the current schema. The item description says `ArtifactManifest model or artifact entry schema` which suggests the author was uncertain.\\n\\n**Gap 2 \u2014 `artifact_list` filter capability**: Whether `artifact_list` supports filtering by artifact type (`codebase-analysis`) to locate the prior artifact must be verified before writing the agent logic.\\n\\n**Gap 3 \u2014 Issue anchoring mechanism**: The item says to anchor codebase-analysis artifacts to a GitHub issue but does not specify which issue (project-level or feature issue). This decision affects the `artifact_register` call signature.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `ArtifactEntry` (or equivalent model in `backlog_core/models.py`) has a `commit_sha: str | None` field\\n- [ ] `codebase-analyzer` agent checks `artifact_list` for a prior `codebase-analysis` artifact before starting a full run\\n- [ ] If prior artifact found with stored `commit_sha`, agent runs `git diff {sha}..HEAD --name-only` and processes only changed files\\n- [ ] Excluded path patterns honoured: `~/.dh/`, `.claude/`, `plan/`, `*.backup`, `*.original`, `research/`\\n- [ ] `--full` override bypasses incremental logic and forces full re-analysis\\n- [ ] `commit_sha` updated to HEAD SHA after each successful analysis\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest tests/ -k codebase` passes (or equivalent test that verifies incremental path)\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` exits 0 after schema change\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n1. Should `commit_sha` be added to `ArtifactEntry` directly, or to a separate metadata dict on the artifact? (Schema change vs. metadata field avoids migration concerns)\\n2. Which GitHub issue should codebase-analysis artifacts be anchored to when no feature issue exists? (A dedicated project-level issue, or a convention like issue #1?)\\n3. Is `--full` a CLI flag for the `codebase-analyzer` agent, or an env var, or a parameter passed in the agent prompt?\\n\\n## Scope Of Changes\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `ArtifactManifest` model or artifact entry schema: add `commit_sha` field to artifact metadata\\n- `codebase-analyzer` agent prompt: add differential analysis logic (check \u2192 diff \u2192 incremental update vs full)\\n- File exclusion patterns: `~/.dh/`, `.claude/`, `plan/`, `*.backup`, `*.original`, `research/`\\n- Anchor codebase-analysis artifacts to a GitHub issue (project-level issue or the feature issue that triggered the analysis) so they are discoverable via `artifact_list`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `codebase-analyzer` currently re-analyzes the full codebase every time it runs, with no awareness of prior analysis\\n- `codebase-analysis` artifacts have no issue association and are outside the artifact manifest discovery path\\n- No staleness signal exists \u2014 agents cannot tell whether a prior analysis is still valid\\n</div>\\n\\n## Desired Behaviour\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `codebase-analyzer` checks `artifact_list` for an existing `codebase-analysis` artifact before starting\\n2. If found, reads the stored commit SHA from the artifact metadata\\n3. Runs `git diff {sha}..HEAD --name-only` filtered to source files only (excluding `~/.dh/`, `.claude/`, plan artifacts, backup files, generated files)\\n4. Re-analyzes only the changed files (differential update), merges findings into the existing artifact\\n5. Updates the stored commit SHA to HEAD after completion\\n6. Full re-analysis only when no prior artifact exists or when `--full` flag is passed\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"bcc1b1e69803cb3569791b278f4b485306d1ec810f40e267c5654f51d122cc83\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPuk74w\"}"}